    "summary": "Textile consisting of six narrow strip woven cotton lengths, hand sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Ground weave: plain weave: dyed black and white warps and dyed black and white wefts. This creates a cloth with a white back ground crossed by warp and weft stripes creating a regular grid resembling tartan. Each of the grid sections in the central panel contain a group of three obliques in black supplementary weft. At both ends of the textile there is a wide band decorated in a diamond based pattern in black supplementary weft.  \r\n\r\nThe textile is finished in unworked warps.",
